WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.134
Today, not much of

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.036
a response from Texas Republicans

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.771
after the impeachment

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.605
of one of their own,

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.240
Attorney General Ken Paxton.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.075
One of the open ended questions

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.176
will his wife

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.444
who is a state senator,

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.946
recuse herself from the trial

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.547
or will she join her colleagues

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.081
in determining

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:15.782
whether her husband

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.484
gets to stay in office?

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.218
As CNN's Ed

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.086
Lavandera reports, the trial

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:20.553
in the state

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.455
Senate is expected to take place

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:23.656
this summer.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.892
The articles of impeachment,

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.827
the group of Texas House members

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.095
who will present the evidence

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.163
in the trial of Attorney

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:30.830
General Ken

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.564
Paxton

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.600
delivered the articles of impeachment

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.968
to the state Senate.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.970
It's been 106 years

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.738
since the last statewide office

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.807
holder in Texas was impeached.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:41.341
Back then,

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.610
it was a governor named James Ferguson

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.245
who was known as poor.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.312
Lieutenant Governor Dan

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.148
Patrick says a committee of senators

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.349
will establish the rules

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.017
for the trial in the coming weeks.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.253
But beyond that, Patrick is refusing

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.454
to answer questions

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.122
about the fellow Republican

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.157
who he's worked closely

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.958
with since Paxton was elected.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.493
In 2014.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.095
There will be witnesses

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.530
and they will be put under oath

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.798
and they will be cross-examined,

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.332
I'm sure, by both sides.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.600
And it will be a regular trial.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.069
And at the end of that trial,

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.703
once the facts are laid out,

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.305
the senators will vote.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.407
The upcoming summer of impeachment

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.108
in Texas

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.277
is exposing the political fault lines

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.279
within the state's Republican Party.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:20.146
Ken Paxton's

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.981
allies are targeting House Speaker

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.016
David Phelan,

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.818
the Republican who presided over

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.019
the impeachment vote.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.287
Is unapologetic

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.522
about the 20 articles of impeachment

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.224
brought against the attorney general

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.026
and the Texas House spokesman.

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.894
And we sent a strong message

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.229
for the future of Texas.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:36.663
A House

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.464
committee started

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:39.499
investigating Paxton in March

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:42.569
after he requested $3.3 million

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:43.570
in taxpayer

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.805
funds to pay for a legal settlement

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:47.674
stemming from a lawsuit

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.175
brought by whistleblower

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.211
who alleged improper behavior

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.346
involving a prominent campaign donor.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:54.848
The articles of impeachment

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:57.050
go further into a pattern of corruption,

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.418
including bribery,

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.786
obstruction, of justice,

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.087
and allegations

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.822
of an extramarital affair.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:03.823
The attorney general

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.859
has been temporarily removed from office

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.927
and denies any wrongdoing.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.830
This shameful process was curated

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.031
from the start

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.434
as an act of political retribution.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.602
We all love Ken Paxton

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.270
around these parts, right?

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.372
Paxton is hoping to generate grassroots

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:20.306
support like this

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.208
rally held in his home county

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.243
in hopes of winning

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:24.611
over the state senators

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.312
who will decide his fate.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.982
Every politician who supports this deceit

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.517
fall impeachment attempt

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.852
will then flecked

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.587
lasting damage

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.689
on the credibility of the Texas House.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.024
Paxton's wife, Angela

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.692
Paxton, is a state senator,

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.960
and there are calls for her

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.096
to recuse herself from the trial.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:46.533
She has not said what she will do.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.934
A group of 12 House

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.969
representatives will present the evidence

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.371
against Ken Paxton.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.239
The majority of them Republicans.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:54.674
This is about facts

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.042
and this is about evidence.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.244
And at the end of the day,

00:02:59.078 --> 00:02:59.712
my colleagues

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:00.647
and I will not stand

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.248
for public corruption.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:02.949
And that's

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.218
why we're proceeding to a trial

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:07.053
in the Texas Senate.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.155
And Jake, Ken

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.323
Paxton is also accused

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.424
of calling House members

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.892
before the impeachment vote,

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.228
threatening him, threatening them to vote

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.463
for him in that vote.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.432
The lead at the head of the House

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.534
committee that brought the impeachment

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:23.636
articles of impeachment

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.004
against him was asked

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.940
if this could lead to further

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.308
articles of impeachment

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.442
and he would refuse to answer

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.310
that question as well.

